OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775004736
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGSADDAM'S TROOPS "CONTROL
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSOUTH-WESTERN IRAQ"
OL,4,D
OL,5, Reports coming out of southern Iraq say
OL,6, government troops are now in control of
OL,7, the south-west of the country.
OL,9,FRefugees from the area say the city of
OL,10,FSamawah, held by Shi'ite Muslim rebels,
OL,11,Fhas now fallen to the Iraqi army.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FA BBC correspondent says the fall of
OL,14,FSamawah brings to an end rebel hopes
OL,15,Ffor an organised revolt in the south.
OL,17,FMeanwhile, Western journalists taken on
OL,18,Fa tour of the northern oil city of
OL,19,FKirkuk say they found it was firmly in
OL,20,Fthe hands of government forces.
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG01-04-91
OL,23,D]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
